From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Price every PO line from one builder, and make the order status
 dots act.

A distributor PO for CD-20261022-OLOUT arrived showing only "Shipping $47.00 /
Tax $24.40 / Total $71.40" with no price on its single line. The total being
exactly shipping + tax is the tell: the merchandise subtotal resolved to $0.00,
so the arithmetic was right and the *inputs* were empty. The order itself was
priced — its line carries a $449.34 customer price and a $284.39 distributor
cost — so this was never a null price on the order.

Three separate gaps let the dollars fall out:

1. `loadPortions()` mapped each line down to {sku, description, doorStyle, qty}.
   The prices were dropped before the email was ever composed.
2. `DistributorEmailLine` had no price field, and `composeDistributorOrderEmail`
   rendered "qty x sku — description" with no money at all.
3. The CSV was built from those same price-less lines, so NetSuite's Rate and
   Amount columns came out blank.

Nothing anywhere computed subtotal + shipping + tax, so the four surfaces that
show a PO could each disagree: the admin PO table printed customer price with no
subtotal row, `buildOrderEmailText` appended a caller-supplied "Order total"
string, and the emailed PO had no line prices at all.

There is now one builder, `@shared/poDocument`, used by the admin PO view, the PO
PDF, the PO CSV and the emailed PO. It resolves each line's unit price and line
total, always emits Subtotal / Shipping / Sales tax / Total, and computes
Total = subtotal + shipping + tax - discounts. A distributor PO shows OUR COST
(the stored distributor cost, read through the same admin enrichment the order
page uses); the customer price is only a flagged fallback, and a line with no
price stays visible as "no price" with a warning instead of disappearing into a
total that still looks plausible.

Also in this patch:

- "Order verified", "Order shipped" and "Order signed" become actions. Verifying
  stamps the order and emails the customer a short thank-you promising shipping
  information; shipped and signed stamp their own timestamps.
- A separate "order received" acknowledgement, with its own stamp, so accepting
  an order and verifying it are never the same email.
- orderReceivedEmailSentAt / orderReceivedEmailTo on order_requests.

Nothing here sends mail or writes a row on its own: both are administrator
actions behind a confirmation.

Two faults reported from the admin order page after this work started:

- The PO SKU read "cs-cs-cs-db18". It was built with a bare template
  `${distributorCode}-${styleCode}-${distributorSku}`. For Clark and Son all
  three parts start with "CS" (distributor code CS, style code CS, item code
  CS-DB18), so the prefix repeated. `@shared/poSku` now drops a token that has
  already appeared, which leaves every other distributor's SKU byte-for-byte
  unchanged, and `normalizePoSku` repairs SKUs already stored the broken way so
  no data migration is needed.
- Marking an order verified failed with "Order status columns are missing on
  order_requests". That is docs/sql/0227 not having been run, not a broken
  button; the panel now names the SQL file to run instead of showing a generic
  error.

Apply from the cabinet-backend repository root:

    git apply /path/to/cabinet-backend-po-pricing-and-order-status-actions.patch

Requires the shared files this patch adds (shared/poDocument.ts,
shared/orderCustomerEmails.ts, shared/poSku.ts) and
the 0227 and 0249 SQL.
